# Constitution

Detail lives in `.cursor/rules/playwright-conventions.mdc` and skills; this file is the always-on floor.

## MUST

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Role-based locators | `getByRole` → label → text → `testId` in POMs only; no inline locators in specs |
| Web-first assertions | `await expect(locator)` in specs; POMs act, never assert |
| `storageState` auth | `setup` project + saved auth; UI login only when testing login or unauthenticated flows |
| Unique self-cleaning data | `uniqueSuffix(testInfo.testId)` (or equivalent) + cleanup fixture for every created record |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive` on the **test**, not on `test.describe` |

## SHOULD

| Practice | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| Faker factories | Shared factories for repeatable test data when Faker fits; still unique + cleaned up in Didaxis |
| Enums for repeated strings | One source for labels, routes, and API paths used across POMs and specs |
| JSDoc on action methods | POM user-action methods document intent; keep locators obvious from names |

## WON'T

| Refusal | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| XPath | Refuse; rediscover with role + accessible name |
| `waitForTimeout` | Refuse; use web-first expects |
| Hardcoded secrets | Refuse; `.env` / CI secrets / `storageState` only |
| `any` | Refuse; type properly or escalate |
| Weakened assertions | Refuse; deleting or loosening `expect` to go green |
| Healing a real bug | Refuse; bug-reporter path only after triage |
| Tags on `describe` | Refuse; one tag per test instead |

